### ✅ Fixed Sequence Diagram (GitHub-safe)
```markdown
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant Client
  participant Flask as Flask (/ask-gpt)
  participant Router as handle_session_text
  participant Helper as call_sheets_action
  participant Hook as /sheet-action
  participant Adapter as _route_sheet_action
  participant Sheets as Google Sheets API

  Client->>Flask: POST /ask-gpt {"text":"bold header"}
  Flask->>Router: handle_session_text(prompt)
  Router-->>Router: check session.type == SPREADSHEET
  Router->>Helper: call_sheets_action("BoldHeader", {"row_number":1})
  Helper->>Hook: POST /sheet-action {"action":"BoldHeader", ...}
  Hook->>Adapter: normalize payload
  Adapter->>Sheets: apply_bold_header(spreadsheet_id, sheet_title, header_row)
  Sheets-->>Adapter: success / error
  Adapter-->>Hook: {"status":"ok" | "error"}
  Hook-->>Helper: response JSON
  Helper-->>Router: handled, reply
  Router-->>Flask: return reply
  Flask-->>Client: {"reply":"Okay—done."}
---

## ✅ Milestone: Voice → Sheets Action (Bold/Unbold Header v1)

**Date:** 2025-09-07

This marks the first complete end-to-end action cycle from **voice input** to **Google Sheets mutation**:

- **Session control working:** Spreadsheet sessions can be started/stopped via `/control-hook`.
- **Routing fixed:** While in spreadsheet mode, voice bypasses Dialogflow and is handled by the router.
- **Intent resolution added:** Handles `"bold header"` and `"unbold header"` (including ASR mis-hears like “on bold”).
- **Action execution confirmed:** Requests reach Google Sheets API (`batchUpdate`) and toggle header formatting.
- **End-to-end test passed:**  
  Voice → Flask → Router → Intent normalization → `/sheet-action` → Google Sheets API → Bold/Unbold applied → Bot responds “Okay—done.”

This is the **first loop-closure milestone**: a spoken command visibly updates a Google Sheet in real time.
